The vendored CLI under vendor/tastecheck is this project's own code (MIT, checked against
vendor/MANIFEST.json). The plugin imports Hermes (MIT, Nous Research) at runtime from the host
install; none of it is copied here.

desktop/plugin.js bundles the Resonant Field theme (desktop/theme/resonant-field.js, Kyanite
Labs, MIT), which embeds third-party fonts as data URIs:

- Hanken Grotesk (400, 600), SIL Open Font License 1.1.
  Copyright 2021 The Hanken Grotesk Project Authors.
  desktop/theme/licenses/OFL-hankengrotesk.txt
- Bricolage Grotesque (700), SIL Open Font License 1.1.
  Copyright 2022 The Bricolage Grotesque Project Authors.
  desktop/theme/licenses/OFL-bricolagegrotesque.txt

The theme's background textures are greyscale, blurred derivatives of images the author
generated for the Resonant Field project with OpenAI's Codex image generation tool. They are
AI-generated images, not photographs. The MIT licence covers them only to the extent the
author holds rights in them; AI-generated images may carry no copyright at all, and no
warranty of originality is given.
